  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1007 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nStronger cold air advection will occur Friday afternoon into \nFriday night. This should keep highs in the upper 60s to lower \n70s, despite abundant sunshine. Lows should drop into the upper\n30s to lower 40s primarily with northerly winds between 5 and 10\nmph. The winds should keep frost from forming in most areas. During\nthe day on Saturday, cold air advection and some cloud cover will\nkeep highs from climbing above the upper 50s to lower 60s. \n\nWe may be talking about our first taste of temperatures dropping\nto around freezing or just below Saturday night. It will truly\nfeel a bit on the chilly side. \n\nTemperatures begin to moderate slowly Sunday into Monday, as a\nmore zonal flow aloft develops. Highs should climb back into the\nlower 60s while low will remain in the lower 30s to around 40\ndegrees.",
